## 🚀 Quick Start (Local Development)

Get the project running on your local machine in under 5 minutes.

### Prerequisites
- [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) (v18 or higher)
- [PostgreSQL](https://www.postgresql.org/) (v14 or higher)
- [Git](https://git-scm.com/)

### 1. Clone the repository
```bash
git clone https://github.com/sergiumurgescu88-lgtm/mindfind.git
cd mindfind
```

### 2. Setup the Backend
```bash
cd server
npm install

# Create and configure your environment variables
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env: Add your DATABASE_URL and generate a strong JWT_SECRET

# Initialize the database schema
node src/migrate.js

# Start the development server
npm run dev
```

### 3. Setup the Frontend
```bash
cd ../client
npm install
npm run dev
```
🎉 Open [http://localhost:5173](http://localhost:5173) in your browser to see the application in action!

---

## 🗄️ Database Schema Overview

The PostgreSQL database is designed for data integrity and performance:
- **`users`**: Stores authentication data, roles (`client`, `worker`, `admin`), and profile info.
- **`requests`**: Job postings linked to users and categories.
- **`offers`**: Bids submitted by workers for specific requests.
- **`conversations` & `messages`**: Real-time chat history between users.
- **`reviews`**: Ratings and feedback left after job completion.
- **`worker_profiles` & `worker_categories`**: Detailed professional profiles and specializations.

